WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.000
After eight installments and countless action
sequences, the Fast and Furious franchise

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.360
has its first spinoff in Hobbs &amp; Shaw.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.860
Now that we've seen everything this movie
has to offer, we're here to give you the lowdown

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.660
on the best, and worst, things in this chapter
of the saga.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.740
Every installment of the Fast &amp; Furious franchise
has gotten bigger, wilder, and more action-packed

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.040
than the ones before it.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.860
For everyone worried that the absence of Vin
Diesel's Dominic Toretto and his "family"

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.760
would lead to a lull in the action, Hobbs
&amp; Shaw keeps the fists flying and the cars

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.620
racing.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.120
Every single major set piece in the film feels
bigger than the last, as Hobbs and Shaw punch,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.340
kick, and bicker their way across the globe.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.520
Anyone familiar with director David Leitch's
cinematic output could have expected that

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.739
the former stuntman would put together all
sorts of over-the-top action sequences, but

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.300
the co-director of John Wick easily surpasses
all expectations.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.480
There's a palpable sense of glee at the heart
of Hobbs &amp; Shaw, as if Leitch and his team

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.100
can't believe they get to create some of the
wacky stunts they're paid to make.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.740
There are cameos aplenty in Hobbs &amp; Shaw:
WWE wrestler, and Dwayne Johnson's real-life

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.740
cousin, Roman Reigns appears as one of the
Hobbs brothers.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:08.240
Kevin Hart, appearing on screen once again
with his former Central Intelligence co-star

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.560
Johnson, appears in the film as Dinkley, an
over-eager air marshal.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.700
Catastrophe and Deadpool 2 star Rob Delaney
appears as agent Loeb.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.220
Leitch even manages to use his pull as the
director of Deadpool 2 to bring in Ryan Reynolds

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.500
as agent Locke.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.580
While it's a delight to see so many talented
comedic actors, and their appearances provide

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:30.980
some of the funniest parts of the film, unfortunately
they also slow the pacing down to a crawl.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.620
Many of the scenes they appear in drag on
way too long, and seemingly exist in the final

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:39.140
cut just to showcase the A-list talent that
the film attracted.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.560
As funny as Hart, Reynolds, and Delaney are,
their appearances distract from the film more

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.560
than they benefit it.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.580
While some of the cameos in Hobbs &amp; Shaw drag
on a touch too long, Dame Helen Mirren's appearance

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.380
as Queenie Shaw feels far, far too short.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.720
It's a source of near constant delight that
Mirren, one of the greatest and most venerated

00:01:56.729 --> 00:02:01.619
actresses working today, has decided to spend
her time as a trash-talking criminal in the

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.040
Fast &amp; Furious franchise.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.640
In Hobbs &amp; Shaw, Queenie is incarcerated for
unknown reasons, visited occasionally by her

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.660
son, and biding her time until she feels like
breaking out.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:14.780
The credits scene implies a prison break for
the Shaw matriarch, so there's plenty of room

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.120
to hope that Mirren will continue to delight
in whatever future installments she appears

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.120
in.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.880
Vanessa Kirby, who plays Hattie Shaw, is 31
years old.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.420
Hattie's brother in the film, Deckard, is
played by Jason Statham, who is 52.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.420
Throughout the film, we see flashbacks to
the two of them as con artist kids, and they

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.680
look to be about the same age…so how old
is Hattie Shaw supposed to be?

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.780
It's a fairly consistent aspect of action
movies to have a massive difference in age

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:44.150
between the male and female co-stars, but
it's distracting to have Hobbs &amp; Shaw position

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.340
Kirby as more or less the same age as Statham
and Johnson.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:51.120
There's even an ongoing flirtation between
Hattie and Hobbs that ultimately leads to

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.560
a kiss between the two, and Dwayne Johnson
is 47.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.620
"My kind of girl!"

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.820
"I see what you're doing.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.340
Do you think I'm stupid?"

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.840
"Of course I think you're stupid."

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.099
Is Kirby playing a character at least a decade
older than her actual age?

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:06.370
Or is Hattie in her early 30s, too?

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.480
Does it even matter?

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.290
After all, Kirby also smooched 57-year-old
Tom Cruise in Mission Impossible: Fallout,

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.610
so her Hobbs &amp; Shaw casting might be just
to set up another stereotypical May-December

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.060
action movie romance.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.660
Hobbs &amp; Shaw takes plenty of opportunities
to showcase the two muscular men at odds and

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.960
working together, and it's a delight nearly
the entire time.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.819
Whether it's showcasing how the two go about
their very different days in a color-coded

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.260
split-screen or seeing them kick butt together,
their odd couple chemistry is a hoot.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.840
It's also an aspect of the Fast &amp; Furious
franchise that has been missing for a while.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:43.960
2 Fast 2 Furious briefly presents Paul Walker
and Tyrese Gibson as conflicted, equally tough

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:48.209
partners, but that scenario barely lasts for
the length of the film before Walker's character

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:50.280
Brian clearly becomes the leader.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.409
Furthermore, Brian and Dom's brotherly rivalry
in subsequent movies never really has the

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:58.280
serious energy that you need to get invested
in who's the faster or more furious of the

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.080
two.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:03.520
However, Hobbs and Shaw spend the whole movie
trading barbs, punches, and dirty looks.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.660
When they finally team up for the climactic
fight, it feels earned and satisfying.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:12.080
While the film stays pretty thematically true
to the past few iterations of the Fast &amp; Furious

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.020
franchise, Hobbs &amp; Shaw still feels removed
from the main run of films.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.519
Besides a quick line of dialogue referencing
Kurt Russell's Mr. Nobody and some use of

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:24.770
nitrous in the climax, the filmmakers don't
really seem interested in making Hobbs &amp; Shaw

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.720
much of a Fast &amp; Furious film.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.110
In a vacuum, that's perfectly reasonable.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.980
Leitch has said that there's plenty of room
for sequels here, and keeping the focus on

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:37.440
the two leading men and mostly new characters
is a good way to keep that potential open.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.220
Still, in terms of feeling like the same universe
and the same characters we've seen before,

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:47.080
Hobbs &amp; Shaw could easily be an entirely different
film outside of the Fast &amp; Furious franchise.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:51.220
With Dwayne Johnson and Vin Diesel reportedly
at each other's throats on the set of Fate

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.430
of the Furious, and Hobbs &amp; Shaw seeming more
and more like a way to keep Johnson involved

00:04:55.430 --> 00:05:00.250
in the franchise without stepping on Diesel's
toes, the film's uneven tone and relationship

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.900
to its parent franchise feels even stranger.

